  "arb-ready-threshold": "Equivalent in composition: landingReady is the gate's logical output and the core passes 1.0/0.0, so > 0.5 and >= 0.5 cannot differ. Only a unit-level input of exactly 0.5 would tell them apart.",
  "gate-ready-recheck": "The ready expression is only reached when not (no new sample and stale): either a new sample just set lastFresh = clockTime (finite, checked earlier) or the gate is not stale, i.e. clockTime - lastFresh <= 0.5 already holds.",
  "grid-max-step": "A step is only taken when the pixel error exceeds 20 px; with this map the smallest resulting step is sigma_min(map) * (0.50/0.70) * 20 px = 0.0227 m (sigma_min = 0.0015883), so n > 0.005 and n > 0.010 always agree and the clamp result is the same (config-dependent equivalence).",
  "ml-max-nan": "Every call site passes the possibly-NaN value as the first operand and a finite constant second; for a NaN first operand `a >= b` is False and the fallback already returns b, exactly what the NaN branch does."
 },
